  "finding": "Continued training did NOT reduce the small-ring pathology. Neither the per-molecule prevalence (0.420 -> 0.440) nor the per-RING closure-policy shape (0.164 -> 0.188) improved; both edged up, neither significantly. What changed is that molecules got SMALLER (28.72 -> 27.02 heavy atoms) with fewer rings (3.78 -> 3.20) and fewer ring-forming events (3.34 -> 2.78). The modest quality gain (+0.10, z=1.15, not significant) is therefore consistent with shrinking molecules rather than with fixing ring chemistry -- exactly the divergence the per-ring metric exists to detect. Once molecule size is held fixed, ring strain has NO detectable effect on QED at either checkpoint (+0.044+-0.049 and -0.049+-0.043), while size does (-0.026 per heavy atom, |z|~7). The SA strain penalty is real at step 1000 (+0.926+-0.223) and weaker at step 2500 (+0.379+-0.238).",
